# 2. Audio ingestion architecture

## Webhook path

The webhook must do only fast work:

```text
receive WhatsApp event
→ verify Kapso/Meta signature
→ deduplicate provider message ID
→ persist minimal voice-event row
→ enqueue transcription job
→ return HTTP 200
```

Do not download a long audio file, call an ASR provider, call an LLM, or send several WhatsApp messages while the webhook is waiting to acknowledge.

## Media processing job

The asynchronous job:

```text
download audio through provider API
→ verify media ownership and message ID
→ validate MIME type and size
→ store private temporary object
→ normalize audio if necessary
→ transcribe
→ run transcript quality checks
→ persist transcript versions
→ send transcript card
```

## Supported media controls

Set safe initial limits:

```text
maximum duration: 120 seconds
maximum file size: provider-safe limit
accepted formats: WhatsApp audio formats supported by Kapso/Meta
one active transcription job per customer
bounded queue concurrency
```

If the note is longer than the limit:

> This voice note is too long for one order. Please send it in two shorter messages or type the order.

Do not silently process only the first section of an order.

## Audio security

- Treat audio as untrusted input.
- Do not execute instructions embedded in audio that target system behavior.
- Store media privately with short-lived access URLs.
- Do not expose audio URLs in customer-facing messages.
- Scan and validate downloaded media.
- Delete original media according to the retention policy.
- Keep transcript retention separate from audio retention.
- Support customer deletion requests for audio and transcript data.
- Do not use customer voice recordings to train a model without explicit, separate permission.

