# 4. Recommended speech-to-text architecture

## Provider abstraction

Do not hard-code one ASR vendor throughout the order function.

Use:

```text
SpeechProvider interface
OpenAITranscriptionAdapter
DeepgramTranscriptionAdapter
GoogleTranscriptionAdapter, optional
FallbackTranscriptionAdapter
```

Required adapter operations:

```text
transcribe(audio, languageHints, glossary, options)
healthCheck()
classifyFailure()
```

Required result fields:

```text
provider
model
transcript
segments
language
language_confidence
word_confidence, if available
audio_duration_ms
processing_time_ms
provider_request_id
cost_estimate
```

## Recommended starting strategy

Because Alo King already uses OpenAI and has an existing Whisper-oriented design, use a staged approach:

### Baseline

Start with the existing OpenAI transcription path for the first controlled pilot. It reduces integration complexity and gives Alo King a measurable baseline.

### Accuracy benchmark

Run the same Lebanese voice-note evaluation set through:

- the current OpenAI transcription model;
- Deepgram’s Arabic-capable model;
- another candidate such as Google Speech-to-Text or a dialect-performing provider.

Evaluate on actual consented Lebanese recordings, not only generic Arabic samples.

### Production choice

Choose the provider based on a weighted score:

```text
Lebanese accuracy: 40%
Mixed-language accuracy: 20%
Order-item accuracy: 15%
Latency: 10%
Cost: 10%
Reliability and privacy terms: 5%
```

The best provider is not necessarily the one with the best general Arabic benchmark. The correct provider is the one that correctly recognizes Alo King’s real Lebanese restaurant names, quantities, modifiers, villages, and code-switching patterns.

## Do not use streaming unless necessary

A WhatsApp voice note is already a completed recording. Streaming ASR is useful for live calls, but batch transcription is usually simpler for voice notes.

Use streaming only if it materially improves:

- very long recordings;
- partial-progress UX;
- live human support;
- future voice-call products.

For normal 5–30 second WhatsApp notes, prioritize accuracy, language handling, and predictable cost over streaming complexity.

