# 6. Commerce parsing after transcript confirmation

After the customer confirms the transcript, call a typed parser.

## Parser output

```json
{
  "intent": "create_or_edit_basket",
  "vendor_hint": "Al Tahouneh",
  "items": [
    {
      "query": "chicken shawarma",
      "quantity": 2,
      "modifiers": [
        {"query": "no garlic sauce", "type": "remove"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 0.91,
  "ambiguities": [],
  "requires_customer_confirmation": true
}
```

## Entity resolution

The server resolves each candidate against:

```text
vendor scope
active menu version
Arabic name
English name
French name
Arabizi aliases
search aliases
section
availability
options
```

The model may suggest candidates, but the server decides whether a real item exists.

## Multiple interpretations

If there are two plausible matches, ask one question:

> Did you mean **Chicken Shawarma** or **Chicken Tawouk**?

Do not make the customer correct ten items in one giant message. Resolve the most important ambiguity first.

## Order summary

After resolution:

```text
2 × Chicken Shawarma
1 × Fries
3 × Pepsi
No garlic sauce
Extra garlic sauce — clarification required

Subtotal: server-calculated USD and LBP
Delivery: server-calculated USD and LBP
Total: server-calculated USD and LBP
```

The final order still requires the normal **Confirm Order** action.

