# 8. Confidence and safety policy

Use multiple confidence dimensions:

```text
asr_confidence
language_confidence
entity_confidence
quantity_confidence
modifier_confidence
vendor_confidence
```

A high transcript confidence does not mean high order confidence.

## Suggested behavior

| Condition | Behavior |
|---|---|
| Clear speech, clear item, clear quantity | Show transcript confirmation, then continue |
| Clear speech, unclear vendor | Ask vendor choice |
| Clear speech, two menu matches | Ask one item clarification |
| Low quantity confidence | Repeat quantity in clarification |
| Low language confidence | Ask customer to record again or type |
| Contradictory modifiers | Ask which preference is correct |
| Address ambiguity | Ask for pin or landmark confirmation |
| Payment/refund/cancel voice request | Require explicit action button and current-state check |
| Allergy or complaint | Safe response plus human path |
| Very low confidence | Request shorter, clearer note or text |

## Confidence must not be the only safeguard

Even when confidence is high:

```text
voice transcript confirmation
+ server-side menu/entity resolution
+ final basket review
+ explicit order confirmation
```

---

# 9. Latency strategy for voice notes

## Target timeline

```text
0–300 ms: webhook acknowledgement
<1 s: progress message if needed
1–4 s: transcription for short note where provider allows
1–2 s: normalization/entity resolution
<5–8 s: transcript/basket response target
```

Actual performance depends on audio length, provider, network, and queue load.

## Asynchronous user experience

For longer notes:

```text
received
→ transcribing
→ transcript ready
→ clarification or basket
```

Use one progress message maximum. Do not send progress updates every second.

## Audio duration policy

For a voice note under 10 seconds, aim for a single fast transcription job.

For 10–30 seconds, process normally with a timeout budget.

For 30–120 seconds, process asynchronously and show progress.

For more than 120 seconds, ask the customer to split the message.

## Retry policy

Retry ASR only for technical failures, not low-confidence content.

```text
technical failure → bounded retry or fallback provider
low confidence → ask customer to clarify
provider timeout → fallback or human path
invalid media → ask customer to record again
```

Do not send the same transcript card twice if the job is retried.

---

# 10. Cost strategy

## Avoid an expensive model for speech recognition decisions

Use:

```text
ASR provider for transcription
small deterministic normalizer for cleanup
fast model for simple entity extraction
capable model only for ambiguity and complex language
```

Do not send audio to both OpenAI and another ASR provider for every customer.

## Conditional fallback

Primary ASR result goes through quality checks. Use a second provider only when:

- confidence is low;
- a critical quantity is uncertain;
- a restaurant/item cannot be resolved;
- the customer corrects the transcript;
- the primary provider fails;
- the sample is part of an evaluation benchmark.

## Cache safe work

Cache by audio hash and provider/model version:

```text
voice:{sha256_audio}:{provider}:{model}:{language_config}
```

Safe cache uses:

- duplicate webhook delivery;
- provider retry;
- repeated processing of the same media ID;
- evaluation reruns.

Do not use a cached transcript after a new audio file has been recorded.

## Store compact context

Do not send the whole menu and conversation to the model. Send:

```text
confirmed transcript
current vendor candidates
relevant menu search results
current basket
customer language
known safe preferences
```

## Track voice cost

Store:

```text
voice_event_id
provider
model
audio_seconds
transcription_cost
normalization_cost
commerce_model_cost
total_cost
latency
cache_hit
fallback_used
order_created
```

Set per-customer and daily voice budgets to prevent abuse.

