# 12. Multilingual test program

## Build a real Lebanese evaluation set

Collect consented, redacted, synthetic, or volunteer recordings covering:

### Dialect and geography

- Beirut speech;
- Mount Lebanon;
- Chouf;
- Aley;
- Metn/Keserwan;
- Bekaa;
- North/Akkar;
- South/Nabatieh;
- different ages and speaking speeds.

### Language patterns

- Arabic script concepts;
- Arabizi;
- English ordering words;
- French ordering words;
- Arabic-English mix;
- Arabic-French mix;
- three-language sentences;
- restaurant names pronounced in English or French;
- item names borrowed from Turkish, Italian, Armenian, or local usage.

### Audio conditions

- quiet room;
- car;
- street;
- restaurant;
- kitchen noise;
- low microphone;
- fast speech;
- multiple speakers;
- pauses and corrections;
- short and long notes.

## Score the full commerce result

Do not score only word error rate. Score:

```text
language detection
transcript meaning
vendor resolution
item resolution
quantity accuracy
modifier accuracy
address accuracy
no-invented-item rate
no-unsafe-action rate
customer correction rate
order conversion
latency
cost
```

A transcription with a word error may still produce the correct item. A fluent transcript can still produce the wrong quantity. Commerce accuracy matters more than general WER.

## Release thresholds

Set thresholds before production. For example:

```text
critical quantity accuracy: ≥99% on tested set
vendor/item resolution: ≥97%
unsafe direct action: 0
unconfirmed order creation: 0
transcript confirmation bypass: 0
p95 transcription path: within agreed target
```

Adjust thresholds based on real pilot data, but never relax the zero-tolerance safety rules.

