# Final voice-note policy

> **Alo King should understand how Lebanese people actually speak, but it must never pretend that speech recognition is certain when it is not.**

The perfect voice-note system is:

```text
fast webhook acknowledgement
+ asynchronous audio processing
+ multilingual/dialect-capable ASR
+ Lebanese alias and code-switching normalization
+ transcript confirmation
+ server-side menu resolution
+ explicit basket confirmation
+ explicit final order confirmation
+ safe fallbacks
+ measurable accuracy and cost
```

The current repository already has a strong safety foundation: voice transcripts are shown back and acted upon only after the customer taps confirmation. The next major improvements are asynchronous media processing, real Lebanese evaluation data, provider benchmarking, Arabizi/code-switching normalization, and a complete voice-specific data and cost pipeline.
